Z||000010||Seanh||02-24-2001||02:13 PM||||A friend of my partents owns the local Dodge Dealership here, and he was at the race. He told us that they new he was dead when they saw him. He is only 1 of 2 drives who wears a helmet without a bar(s) across the front. He hit is face on the steering wheel or somthing and forced his nose through his head. I dont think they are sure why this happened since his seatbelt should have prevented it. I heard (not a reliable soure) that somthing from his car cut the seatbelt.||||reg||1
Z||000011||Songman||02-25-2001||01:18 PM||||There are so many stories floating around...<P>The seatbelt thing came a few days after the accident and Simpson is pissed about it.. Yes, his was a Simpson.<P>I was at the race in Atlanta about 10 years ago when Grant Adcox was killed. Same thing. Minor accident, dead driver. Grant was a very large man and had loosened his seatbelt to be more comfortable. No fault of the belt.<P>I have seen nothing at all that even hinted that Dale hit his face on the steering wheel. That is almost impossible in these cars. The cause of death was said to be head injuries which is a general term. In this case, specifically it means that when the car stopped so dramatically when it hit the wall, his head kept on moving forward at 180 mph and then snapped back when it reached the maximum forward position and breaking his neck.<P>NASCAR has seen this problem and devised a safety precaution for it. Dale chose not to wear it. It is a piece that fits around the neck and snaps to the helmet and the rollbar. Some drivers don't like it because it is hard to get out of in case of fire. Had Dale been wearing this piece of equipment he most likely would still be alive.<P>I was on the road when I learned of his death and have remained pretty much in shock for days. NASCAR has definitely lost it biggest legend. But he did go out doing what he loved and happy that he had two of his cars in front of him...<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000012||Black88GT||02-25-2001||03:17 PM||||Dale's face didn't hit the steering wheel, well not exactly.  His chin hit the steering wheel and the force of impact was transmitted to his brain and it snapped his neck.  Thats what they just showed on ESPN with a doctor illustrating everything, so I trust that account.||||reg||1
